@@ -8,22 +8,43 @@ npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH cha
 npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is:
+
+```json
+{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "status": "todo", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }
+```
+
+`status` is `"todo"` (the default), `"doing"` or `"done"`. Any other value answers 400
+`{ "error": "status must be todo, doing or done" }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?status=todo\|doing\|done` keeps the tasks in that status (deprecated: `?done=true` keeps the done ones, `?done=false` the `todo` and `doing` ones) | 200, an array of tasks, or 400 for an unknown value |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "status": "todo" }` (`status` optional, `todo` by default) | 201, the task, or 400 |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `status` | 200, the task, 400 or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
+### `done` is deprecated
+
+`done` (a boolean) was replaced by `status`. For one release it still works, and it will be removed in the next one:
+
+- Every task still has `done`, `true` exactly when `status` is `done`.
+- `POST` and `PATCH` still accept `done: true` (status `done`) and `done: false` (status `todo`, even from `doing`).
+  A `done` that is not a boolean answers 400 `{ "error": "done must be a boolean" }`.
+- `GET /api/tasks?done=true` and `?done=false` still filter (`false` means `todo` or `doing`); any other value answers
+  400 `{ "error": "done must be true or false" }`.
+- When a request sends both `status` and `done` (in the body or the query), `status` wins.
+
+Existing databases are migrated on startup: `done = 1` becomes status `done`, `done = 0` becomes `todo`, and the `done`
+column is dropped. Back up a production database before upgrading, since that cannot be undone.
+
 ## Layout
 
 - `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
